  1325	     serialization sort key: RRSIGs sort by (key tag, inception, expiration, signature bytes, canonical RRSIG
  1326	     RDATA). A duplicate is an RR identical in owner, class, type and RDATA (`SNAPSHOT_FORMAT`); TTL consistency
  1327	     within an RRset is checked separately (point 2).
  1328	   - **Raw time fields in sort keys.** Inception and expiration in these sort keys, and in the G35 candidate tuple
  1329	     (section 7.3), are the raw 32-bit unsigned RRSIG field values compared numerically (equivalently, as
   137	### The 4 December test and build evidence
   138	
   139	| Word | Meaning | Do not use |
   140	|---|---|---|
   141	| relying-party test | The registered test on 4 December 2026. One independent person uses only V1's documentation to decide each case of the registered mapping. | usability test |
   142	| registered mapping | The registered list of test cases, with the expected verdict and the safe decision for each case. | scenario set |
   143	| unsafe accept | A decision to rely on a claim that the evidence does not establish. It can concern a VALID receipt. | bad accept |
   144	| false reject | A decision to reject an honest receipt. | — |
   145	| independence conditions | The registered conditions for the test person: a computing background, no knowledge of this field or project, no talk with the author about Tessera, and no help during the test. | — |
   146	| negative control | A test that must fail for a program with a known defect. It shows that the test can find that defect. | — |
   147	| companion verifier | A verifier with one deliberate defect, made for a negative control. | broken verifier |
   547	
   548	C4(i) needs a DNSSEC-authenticated record that binds V1's two keys to D. Neither the spec nor wamason.com has one
   549	yet (spike report; R-4.26 says only "DNSSEC records publishing the fingerprints").
   550	
   551	**Owner name:** `_tessera-v1.<D>`, where D is `common.issuer`.
   552	- The verifier rebuilds this name from the signed `issuer` and compares it, label by label and ignoring ASCII
   553	  case, with the validated RRset's owner name. Anything else gives `DNS_OWNER`.
   554	- *Reason:* the owner name itself is then the C4 owner-name check (G-21/M2). An underscore label cannot collide
   555	  with a hostname, and the `-v1` suffix lets a later profile publish next to it.
   620	  inverse is the parse. `:` is outside the separators, and `DNS_WINDOW` and `DNS_WINDOW_LENGTH` are checks on parsed
   621	  values, so none of them affects the split.
   622	- One RR with one character-string removes concatenation ambiguity. The RDATA length byte delimits the string.
   623	- The owner name is compared as a label sequence, so `_tessera-v1.wamason.com` cannot match
   624	  `_tessera-v1.wamason.com.evil.example` or `tessera-v1.wamason.com` (XD-12 to XD-14).
   625	- The value begins `v=` (0x76), while every tagged string in §2 begins with a byte from 0x11 to 0x1d. So a TXT
   626	  value can never be a V1 frame, and a frame can never be a TXT value.

